<h4>D. Be a Witness to the Truth</h4>
<p>Choose one specific, concrete action this week to bear witness to the truth. Ideas: (1) Defend someone who is being spoken ill of behind their back &mdash;say something good about them instead. (2) Correct a falsehood you see spreading online with charity and facts. (3) Tell someone the truth in love about something they need to hear, even if it is hard. (4) If you are in a situation where everyone is lying or cheating (work, school), refuse to participate and explain why &mdash;quietly, without self-righteousness. Write your commitment:</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">My concrete action this week: _______________________________</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">I will do it on (day): ________________________</p>

<h4>E. Study the Martyrs of Truth</h4>
<p>Research one of the following martyrs who died for the truth: St. Thomas More (refused to swear a false oath), St. John the Baptist (beheaded for telling Herod the truth about his marriage), St. John Nepomucene (patron of the confessional seal; killed for refusing to reveal what the queen confessed), St. Maria Goretti (died defending her purity and the truth about human dignity). Write a paragraph: What did this saint refuse to do? What was the cost? What does their witness say to you?</p>
